# x-pcaccess-desktop: desktop wiring (applied by the wiring task; these files are not owned by it)

1. apps/desktop/src/shared/core-lanes/desktop-operation-route.ts, OPERATION_ROUTES, "// remote access" block: add
     pcAccessReadiness: positional('pcAccess/readiness', []),
     pcAccessApprove: positional('pcAccess/approve', []),
   (and the two names in desktop-operation-route.test.mjs's table; ipc-computer.ts calls them through invokeDesktopOperation).
2. apps/desktop/src/main/ipc.ts, registerComputerIpc call: pass `invokeDesktopOperation`
     registerComputerIpc({ handle, shell, computer, invokeDesktopOperation });
   and drop the `pcAccess: computer?.pcAccess,` line of the registerSessionIpc call (ipc-sessions.ts no longer takes it).
3. apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts: remove the `pcAccess: windowsPcAccess(),` entry of the `computer:` option passed to the IPC
   registration, and the REMOTE_CONTROLLER_KEY_DELIVERED_EVENT and REMOTE_CONTROLLER_KEYS_OWED_EVENT handlers in the
   desktop-event listener with their two imports (the core's PcAccessService enrolls on delivery and revokes owed keys).
   KEEP windowsPcAccess(), the `pcAccess` variable and the createPcAccess / pendingRevokesFile / PcAccess imports: the phone
   screen's `pcAccess.approveWithCredential` (createScreenSourceHost options) still calls windowsPcAccess() until
   s3-screen-source / x-screen-source-desktop moves it to the core's approve_with_credential (that task then deletes them);
   until then it is the only remaining user of the TS queue, so two installer queues coexist for the phone password path only.
